  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 359 AM CDT Thu Jun 18 2026\n\nA deeper 500 MB trough will cross the region from late Saturday into \nSunday, bringing renewed rain chances to at least parts of Iowa. \nHowever, longer-range models remain divided on the track and \nevolution of this system, with the GFS initiating convection farther \nsouth in Nebraska and more rigorously than the ECMWF, resulting in \nan apparent MCS affecting parts of Kansas, Missouri, and perhaps \nsouthern Iowa. Meanwhile the ECMWF has a broader and more northward \nsolution depicting widespread rain across Iowa. For now will \nmaintain the areawide 60-80% PoPs initiated by the NBM and monitor \nmodel trends in the coming days. Early next week there are \nindications that another trough may cross the region, but at this \nrange details are even less clear.",
